  "basis": "Exact-QID way758796818 supplies a76.881m by4.285m plan. Current PMTiles footway35185052559676,west steps35184485842300 and east path35184485842310 establish alignment. Anchor[21.03004965,39.4605618],heading0.369628459904: +X northeast/eastern bank,-X southwest/western bank,+Z southeast,-Z northwest. Three ordinary views establish the present reconstructed bridge,the main crown offset toward the shorter western bank and both relief openings. The tested normal Mercator detail tile is17/73192/49876,236.05657005461086m wide,using public semantic overzoom and retained standard Mapzen samples. Native viewer water datum257.3589782714844m and end heights11.44/5.8m above it are map/photo approximations,not surveyed elevations.",
  "fit": "All five loaded tiers preserve the one independent building,six independent transportation records,all11 raw road inputs,rawDEM and water. The mapped bridge replacement reduces11to10 nonempty rendered road records. Six transverse end samples stay within0.015000m of the authored end datum. End aprons extend0.3m into mapped approaches; the trails turn,so straight bank-extension probes are diagnostic rather than a false requirement that trails continue straight. Three bounded rendered-ground masks cap high coarse bank terrain at0.75m model-local height. Horizontal rays through all three local portals clear the model and rendered ground,with outside-ground probes unchanged. The western relief remains obscured by coarse bank terrain in distant views; hard bank terraces,water/tile boundary steps and generated path-support walls remain visible. Nearby rock faces,customs house,vegetation and trails are outside this bridge model. This is scoped approximate placement at detail tile17; coarser water datums are unverified. Failed loading retains all11 road records and native ground/water; unloading restores ground and disposes model/support geometry.",
